{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3169","artifact_type":"audit-report","name":"doc-drift-audit-3169@sha256:23c121e5e820dc3e17288365af7bbcce62f4dd8ad0250f22debcf4f3bd51ed3d"},"owner_reference":"3169","content":"# Documentation Drift Audit \u2014 content-based duplicate detection (#3169)\n\nPlan: Pdc6d1abd (feature), P6f00dc1c/T4 (this quality gate task)\nFeature commits audited: 44873fa9c..24138d3b8 on fix/backlog-sync-retryable-network-errors\nHEAD at audit time: ed403174ec694dc632ad1dc891157ff3249d1692\n\n## Method\n\nVerified every doc claim about content-based duplicate detection against current code:\n`backlog_core/search.py` (`find_content_duplicates`, `build_concept_query`, `DuplicateCheckStatus`,\n`ContentDuplicateMatch`), `backlog_core/operations.py` (`_classify_duplicate_check`,\n`_check_for_duplicates`, `list_items`), `backlog_core/models.py` (`DuplicateItemError`),\n`backlog_core/server.py` (`backlog_add`/`backlog_list` MCP tools), and `sam_schema/backlog.py`\n(CLI `backlog add --force`, `backlog list --search`). Also grepped the whole plugin for residual\nfuzzy/threshold/difflib/SequenceMatcher references and for stale \"no --search flag\" claims.\n\nDocs known to have been touched by this feature's own T7 (docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md,\nskills/backlog/SKILL.md, skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md,\nbacklog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md) and T8 (docs/dh-workflow-graph.json, dh-workflow-explorer.html date\nbump) were re-verified independently rather than trusted as complete.\n\n## Findings\n\n### F1 \u2014 skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md:35 \u2014 stale \"no --search flag\" claim\n\nText: \"the CLI has no `--search` full-text flag, but these two are fully supported\" (referring to\n`--section`/`--title`).\n\nThis is now false. Commit `67e5a7823` (\"feat(backlog_core): add search filtering to list_items and\nCLI backlog list --search\") added a `--search` option to `sam_schema/backlog.py`'s `list_items`\nTyper command, wired to `operations.list_items(search=...)` \u2192\n`backlog_core.search.apply_search_filter`. `uv run sam_schema/cli.py backlog list --search \"...\"`\nworks today. Not touched by T7/T8. Update the parenthetical to state the CLI now supports\n`--search` (full-text, same syntax as MCP `backlog_list(search=...)`).\n\n### F2 \u2014 skills/backlog/README.md:249-251 \u2014 stale \"no --search flag\" claim\n\nText: \"Note: the CLI's `backlog list` has no `--search` flag \u2014 full-text search ... has no CLI path\nas of 2026-08-05 (backlog item #2793). Use the MCP `backlog_list(search=...)` tool for full-text\nsearch.\"\n\nSame root cause as F1 \u2014 this feature's own commit `67e5a7823` added the CLI `--search` flag,\nmaking this note stale. Not touched by T7/T8. This is a **separate** drift from the pre-existing\nfuzzy-language drift in this same file (see \"Out of scope\" below) \u2014 it needs its own fix: remove\nor correct the note to reflect that `backlog list --search` is now supported.\n\n### F3 \u2014 skills/groom-backlog-item/references/issue-classification.md:86 \u2014 stale \"no --search flag\" claim\n\nText: \"(the CLI's `backlog list` has no `--search` full-text flag, but `--status` used here is fully\nsupported)\". Same false claim as F1/F2, same root cause. Not touched by T7/T8.\n\n### F4 \u2014 skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:91 \u2014 concept extraction source understated\n\nStep 3 says \"Extract 2 to 4 key concepts from `title`.\" only. The mirrored implementation,\n`build_concept_query(title, description)` in `backlog_core/search.py`, extracts concepts from\n`f\"{title} {description}\"` (both fields) \u2014 confirmed also by `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:407`\n(\"extracts up to 4 significant words ... from title + description\"). The search.py docstring\nexplicitly states this function \"Mirrors the manual concept-extraction step already prescribed by\n`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` Step 3\", so the doc and code are\nmeant to match \u2014 currently the doc undersells the input scope. Update Step 3 to say \"from `title`\nand `description`\". T7's commit `284f23bb1` only added the CLI-parity line to this file; it did not\ntouch this step's wording.\n\n## Out of scope \u2014 confirmed still true, tracked separately as #3300\n\nskills/backlog/README.md carries stale fuzzy-duplicate-detection language unrelated to F2 above:\n- Line 31: example filename `p1-add-fuzzy-duplicate-detection.md`\n- Line 203: `force=False,  # skip fuzzy duplicate check`\n- Line 217: `# add --force to skip the fuzzy duplicate check`\n- Lines 389, 394, 406, 411: illustrative \"Added fuzzy title matching...\" / \"Fuzzy threshold of 0.85...\" example content\n\nVerified these lines are still present and unchanged. Per the dispatch instructions this is\ntracked as backlog item #3300 and is explicitly out of scope for this audit \u2014 reported here only\nto confirm the tracked drift is real and current, not to duplicate #3300's scope. Not counted in\nTotal findings below.\n\n## Verified clean (no drift found)\n\n- `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 Step 3 language (\"Content-scoped token/boolean match across\n  title, description, and section bodies\") matches `find_content_duplicates` behavior exactly.\n- `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` \u2014 `force` field description (\"Skip content-based duplicate check\")\n  matches `server.py:1250` and `sam_schema/backlog.py`.\n- `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u00a7Module: search.py \u2014 fully accurate against current\n  `search.py`/`operations.py` implementation, including exports list, tri-state\n  `DuplicateCheckStatus`, and the ADR-004 replacement note. No stale `parsing.py` fuzzy-matcher\n  residue found (grepped for fuzzy/ratio/SequenceMatcher/difflib in `parsing.py`).\n- `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` / `dh-workflow-explorer.html` \u2014 T8's diff is a one-line\n  regeneration-date bump only; no duplicate-detection-specific graph content to drift.\n- `backlog_core/server.py` MCP tool docstrings (`backlog_add`, `backlog_close` dismissal reasons)\n  \u2014 accurate, no fuzzy/threshold language.\n- No remaining `difflib`/`SequenceMatcher`/`SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD` references tied to duplicate\n  detection outside of an unrelated filter-name-suggestion helper in `server.py` and an unrelated\n  migration-fidelity diff script.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nF1-F3 share one root cause (the CLI `--search` flag added by this feature) and can be fixed in a\nsingle small doc pass \u2014 replace the three \"no --search flag\" notes with a short statement that\n`backlog list --search` is supported (same query syntax as MCP `backlog_list(search=...)`). F4 is\na one-line wording fix in start.md Step 3.\n\nTotal findings: 4\n"}